Understand assets and liabilities

Learn how things you own and obligations you owe affect your finances. Focus on building net worth, not just displaying an expensive lifestyle.

Think beyond your salary

Employment can provide stability and skills. Entrepreneurship, investments and other income sources may help build wealth, but each involves different risks.

Develop business skills

Learn to identify problems, create value, communicate, negotiate and manage resources. Wealth creation is not just about picking investments.

Manage risk intelligently

Avoid confusing confidence with certainty. Understand downside risk, diversification, liquidity and the consequences of borrowing before investing.

Take responsibility for your financial future

Build habits and skills that give you more choices over time, rather than depending entirely on circumstances outside your control.

## 2. The two authors' perspectives

- Donald Trump: Emphasizes real estate, deal-making, negotiation, business ownership and leveraging opportunities.
- Robert Kiyosaki: Emphasizes financial literacy, cash flow, assets, liabilities and entrepreneurship.

Their shared message is to learn how wealth works instead of relying solely on conventional assumptions about money.&#x20;

