## 3. Important cautions

This is a perspective on wealth creation, not a guaranteed formula for becoming rich.

- Real estate is not automatically a profitable asset; costs, debt and cash flow matter.
- Borrowing magnifies losses as well as gains.
- Not every person needs to become an entrepreneur.
- A stable job, emergency savings and diversified investments can be sensible parts of a financial plan.
- The authors' views on investing should be evaluated independently rather than followed blindly.

## 4. Your practical action plan

As a computer science student preparing for placements, your first objective should be to increase your earning potential while developing sound financial habits.

## Financial independence checklist

0/7

Track all spending for 30 days.

Learn the difference between assets, liabilities, income and expenses.

Build job-ready technical skills that can increase your earning potential.

Save a portion of any income you receive, according to your circumstances.

Learn about emergency funds, inflation, compounding and diversified investing.

Research an investment thoroughly before risking real money.

Review your finances monthly and set one measurable financial goal.

## The one-sentence summary

Don't focus only on earning more money; learn to manage it, understand risk, create value and gradually build assets that support your financial goals.



